senses.gloss:
लज्ज् LAJJ, Ⅰ. (P.) Ā. lajja, be ashamed, 🞄before (ab.), of (any one, in., rarely g.;
 🞄a thing, in.), to (inf.): pp. lajjita, embarrassed, 🞄ashamed, of (any one, in., anything, 🞄—˚);
 bashful;
 cs. P. lajjaya, cause any one 🞄to be ashamed, inspire with shame. vi, be 🞄ashamed, to (inf.): pp. ashamed, at (—˚). 🞄sam, be ashamed.

लज्जा lajj-ā, f. shame, bashfulness, embarrassment;
 🞄being ashamed of (—˚): yuvāṃ -me kā lajjā, why should I be ashamed of 🞄you? -kara, a. (ī) causing shame, disgraceful, 🞄to (—˚);
 -ākṛti, a. feigning shame.

लज्जायित lajjā-y-i-ta, den. pp. ashamed;
 🞄embarrassed;
 n. embarrassment (pl.).

लज्जावत् lajjā-vat, a. bashful;
 embarrassed;
 🞄-śīla, a. id.;
 -āvaha, a. shameful.
